ramdocs-0013-a0-conflict,ramdocs_a,"Who is the artist of the album ""A Kind of Hush""?",misinfo,,,Carpenters,,The Beatles,,,,0,,,Carpenters,correct,,,,"A Kind of Hush (album) A Kind of Hush is the seventh studio album by American popular music duo Carpenters. It was released in June 11, 1976. By the time of the album's recording, Richard Carpenter's addiction to sleeping pills had begun to affect him professionally, and he blames this for the album being, in his opinion, sub-par. All three excerpted singles became hits. ""There's a Kind of Hush (All Over the World)"", a cover of a 1960s song by Herman's Hermits, broke both the UK Top 30 and US Top 20, as well as topping the adult contemporary chart.",
