ramdocs-0139-a0-conflict,ramdocs_a,What is the population of Port Vincent?,misinfo,,,741,,"1,234",,,,0,,,741,correct,,,,"Port Vincent, Louisiana Port Vincent is a village in Livingston Parish, Louisiana, United States. The population was 741 at the 2010 census. It is part of the Baton Rouge Metropolitan Statistical Area. Port Vincent is located at (30.337250, -90.841927). According to the United States Census Bureau, the village has a total area of 1.7 square miles (4.4 km²), of which 1.6 square miles (4.3 km²) is land and 0.04 square mile (0.1 km²) (2.37%) is water. As of the census of 2000, there were 463 people, 192 households, and 134 families residing in the village. The population density was 280.3",
