ramdocs-0201-a0-conflict,ramdocs_a,Who is the architect of the Kidd House?,misinfo,,,Leila Ross Wilburn,,Frank Lloyd Wright,,,,0,,,Leila Ross Wilburn,correct,,,,"Kidd House (Lavonia, Georgia) The Kidd House in Lavonia, Georgia, also known as Kidd Residence was built in 1919. It is a -story bungalow house with Craftsman interior details. It was designed by architect Leila Ross Wilburn. In a survey of historic resources in Lavonia, the house with its pecan grove were found to be significant architecturally ""as one of the most elaborate examples of Craftsman/Bungalow design"" in the area, and also as an example of a small farmstead in the city, and also for its association with C.A. Kidd, Sr. It was listed on the National Register of Historic",
