ramdocs-0240-a0-conflict,ramdocs_a,What is the gender composition of Wirral Grammar School?,misinfo,,,Boys,,Girls | Girls,,,,3,,,Boys,correct,,,,"Wirral Grammar School for Girls Wirral Grammar School for Girls is an all-girls grammar school on the Wirral Peninsula, Merseyside, England. It is on Heath Road, Bebington, on the Wirral Peninsula, England, next door to Wirral Grammar School for Boys. The school consists of lower school (ages 11–16) and Sixth Form (ages 17–18), and entrance is by the 11-plus examination. Mrs Elaine Cogan has been its head teacher since 2001. Consistently high achieving, Wirral Grammar School for Girls has been designated as a ""high performing school"" by the Specialist Schools Academies Trust and has received an Ofsted rating of 'Outstanding'",
