ramdocs-0263-a0-conflict,ramdocs_a,When was Sunshine Records established?,misinfo,,,late 1964,,early 1970,,,,0,,,late 1964,correct,,,,"Sunshine Records (Australia) Sunshine Records was an Australian independent pop music record label of the mid-1960s. It was established in late 1964 by promoter Ivan Dayman in collaboration with musician-producer-arranger-songwriter Pat Aulton and entrepreneur, producer and songwriter Nat Kipner (who subsequently founded the Spin Records label). Although his enterprise was short-lived, Dayman was arguably the first Australian popular music entrepreneur to create a fully integrated pop music company that included artist management and bookings, record production, record labels, venue management and concert promotion. Most of the label's releases were made in the period 1965-67. Its biggest act was solo singer",
ramdocs-0263-a0-conflict,ramdocs_a,When was Sunshine Records established?,misinfo,,,late 1964,,early 1970,,,,1,,,early 1970,conflict,,,,"Sunshine Records (Australia) Sunshine Records was an Australian independent pop music record label of the mid-1960s. It was established in early 1970 by promoter Ivan Dayman in collaboration with musician-producer-arranger-songwriter Pat Aulton and entrepreneur, producer and songwriter Nat Kipner (who subsequently founded the Spin Records label). Although his enterprise was short-lived, Dayman was arguably the first Australian popular music entrepreneur to create a fully integrated pop music company that included artist management and bookings, record production, record labels, venue management and concert promotion. Most of the label's releases were made in the period 1970-72. Its biggest act was solo singer.",
