ramdocs-0278-a1-conflict,ramdocs_a,Where is the News Democrat published?,misinfo,,,"Russellville, Kentucky",,"Springfield, Illinois",,,,0,,,"Russellville, Kentucky",correct,,,,"News-Democrat & Leader The News-Democrat & Leader is a twice-weekly newspaper in Russellville, Kentucky. It has been published since 1806, fourteen years after Kentucky became a state. Russellville is the county seat of Logan County. The current title was formed with the merging of ""The Logan County News"" and ""The Democrat"" in 1911. Then in 1968, employees of the ""News-Democrat"" started a paper called ""The Logan Leader"". A few months later, this was merged back into the original company, which published the papers under different names each week. In the 1990s, this was changed to a publication under the combined",
