ramdocs-0358-a2-conflict,ramdocs_a,When was Christ Lutheran Church founded?,misinfo,,,1862,,1920,,,,0,,,1862,correct,,,,"Christ Lutheran Church (Ellenville, New York) Christ Lutheran Church and Parsonage, originally the German Evangelical Lutheran Church of Ellenville, is a historic Lutheran church and parsonage located at Ellenville, Ulster County, New York. The church was built in 1862 in the Greek Revival style. It was moved, enlarged, reoriented, and completely remodeled in 1903–1904 in the Gothic Revival style when moved to its present location. It is a roughly L-shaped building, with a T-shaped main block consisting of a -story, gable-roofed front block and -story gable-roofed rear block. Appended to it is a 1-story addition. It features a two-tiered, square",
