ramdocs-0367-a1-conflict,ramdocs_a,What is the primary political ideology of National Action?,misinfo,,,Right-wing,,Liberal | Liberal,,,,0,,,Right-wing,correct,,,,"National Action (Malta) National Action (, AN) was a right-wing Maltese political party active between 2007 and 2010. The party was founded in June 2007, the two most prominent founders being Josie Muscat, a medical doctor and entrepreneur and a former MP of the Nationalist Party, and real estate magnate Anġlu Xuereb. Muscat was elected National Action's first Leader. The party was best known for its position on immigration. It believed that Malta should close its borders to illegal immigration and, where this is not possible, the European Union (of which Malta is a member) should be obliged to share",
