ramdocs-0393-a2-conflict,ramdocs_a,Who was Chilperic's father?,misinfo,,,Childeric II,,Lothair I | Guntram,,,,0,,,Childeric II,correct,,,,"Chilperic II Chilperic II (c. 672 – 13 February 721), known as Daniel prior to his coronation, was the youngest son of Childeric II and his half-cousin, king of Neustria from 715 and sole king of the Franks from 718 until his death. As an infant, he was spirited to a monastery to protect his life from the internecine feuding of his family. There, he was raised as Daniel until the death of Dagobert III in 715, when he was taken from the monastery — at the age of forty-three — and raised on the shield of the Neustrian warriors",
