ramdocs-0406-a0-conflict,ramdocs_a,302 Squadron was formed in which year?,misinfo,,,"October 1st, 1974",,"January 1st, 1950",,,,0,,,"October 1st, 1974",correct,,,,"The squadron was formed on October 1st, 1974 at Chitose Air Base in Hokkaido as the second of the JASDF's F-4 Phantom squadrons. It was the first operational unit to operate the F-4, the 301st being the first training unit. It also operated Lockheed T-33A trainer/liaison aircraft. On September 6, 1976 two F-4EJ's of the squadron were scrambled from Chitose to intercept the MiG-25 of Viktor Belenko who had flown into Japanese territory to defect. They were unable to intercept him, which led to changes in the Japanese air defense system. On November 26, 1985 the squadron transferred to Naha",
