ramdocs-0442-a0-conflict,ramdocs_a,When was Carl Roth born?,misinfo,,,"November 18, 1797",,"January 1, 1800",,,,0,,,"November 18, 1797",correct,,,,"Carl Reinhold Roth Carl Reinhold Roth was a Swedish businessman and ironmaster who lived during the late 17th to mid 18th century. He is best known as the first ironmaster named Roth at the ironworks in Ludvika, Sweden. Reinhold was in his time one of Stockholm's more prominent businessmen. He also owned Sunnansjö ironworks and estate, and Skogsegen (Judge Hörneåfor’s ironworks in Västerbotten), devoted himself to the nascent sawmill industry, and was ship-owner of the Augusta (named for his second wife). Reinhold was born November 18, 1797 in Lower Fösked. His career began in Stockholm, where he was employed by",
