ramdocs-0442-a1-conflict,ramdocs_a,When was Carl Roth born?,misinfo,,,"October 12, 1753",,"January 1, 1800",,,,0,,,"October 12, 1753",correct,,,,"Carl Roth II Carl Roth II was a Swedish ironmaster who lived between the 17th and 18th centuries. He is best known for owning two ironworks in Karlstad Municipality, Värmland County, Sweden: Duvnäs (Duvenäs), and Nedre Fösked (Föske). Carl was born on October 12, 1753, in Stockholm. On June 26, 1764, at the age of 10, he enrolled at Uppsala University under Stockholm's Nation. After graduating in 1771, he moved with his parents to their estate at Duvnäs where he focused primarily on agriculture and working at the family's mill. Carl was said to have a Godly and humble disposition",
